[00:31.30]There is a special event called an Einschulung.
[00:35.06]Everyone in the family meets to give the child presents, like pens and books, for their new school life.
[00:42.84]For the first day of school, parents give their children a large paper cone called a Schultüte.
[00:50.20]Inside there are things for school and sweets.
[00:59.44]In traditional Japanese houses you often find a butsudan.
[01:04.90]A butsudan is a special place where you go to remember your dead relatives.
[01:10.92]People usually put things on the butsudan for their ancestors: a book, some flowers or a bowl of rice, for example.
[01:19.92]Adults also tell stories about these people to their children so they are not forgotten.
[01:30.60]Pets are popular in many cultures around the world.
[01:34.96]Looking after an animal helps a child learn how to be responsible.
